At some time point, all three: ObjectA, ObjectB, ObjectC are intended for destruction and are not needed any more in the application and then each calls Dispose() as they implement IDisposable interface. When Dispose() is called their collections which held SpecialProperties are cleared out (and so from now on no one is referencing any of these 60,000 SpecialProperties)

Are these 60,000 SpecialProperties going to be garbage collected as soon as possible even if specialManagerSingletonRef won't be set to null?

I am not sure how this static member which is holding reference to SpecialManagerSingleton may affect garbage collection as from what logic tells me every object which has reference to other won't be garbage collected and without nulling the specialManagerSingletonRef we may have a memory leak then (or at least until the singleton's classloader is eligible for collection which in this case will be at the time of application closing!). But maybe GC will treat this scenario differently?

